  "subject": "a ten-year-old boy covering his new term's textbooks with plastic book covers the night before school starts, the plastic bubbling no matter what, until he gives every bubble a name and starts the new year proud of them",
  "caption": "Mandarin electro-swing, 1930s swing meets modern house. Punchy swing horn section riffs, walking upright bass, four-on-the-floor house kick under brushed swing snare, bouncing honky-tonk piano, clarinet runs. Vintage gramophone crackle over a modern punchy low end. Male baritone, playful crooner phrasing with spoken asides. 124 BPM, C minor. Bouncy, cheeky and playful. No trap beats, no dubstep drop, no autotune, no rock guitar, no ballad strings.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - gramophone crackle, horn riff, house kick enters]\n\n[Verse 1]\n開學前一個晚上\n新課本堆成一座山\n書套一張一張攤開\n我用尺慢慢推\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n推好了這邊\n那邊又鼓起來\n\n[Chorus]\n包書套 包書套\n每本都有小泡泡\n推不平就不推了\n我幫它們取名字\n\n[Verse 2]\n國語課本上是阿胖\n數學課本上是小圓\n自然課本有三個\n叫大哥二哥三哥\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n同學的書平平的\n沒有一個有名字\n\n[Chorus]\n包書套 包書套\n我的書有一家人\n老師問這是什麼\n我說他們來上學\n\n[Outro - clarinet run, horns, crackle fades]",
